      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Ph2acacH (292 mg, 1.30 mmol) and ortho-nitrophenol (181 mg, 1.30 mmol) were combined in methanol (20 mL). Excess triethylamine (5.20 mmol) was slowly added and the mixture was stirred for 1 h at room temperature. A methanol solution (20 mL) of ErCl3 hydrate (1.30 mmol) was added, giving a yellow solution that was stirred overnight at room temperature. A crimson–yellow precipitate was filtered off and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The residue was dissolved in toluene (5 mL), stirred for 2 h, filtered, and slow evaporation of toluene at room temperature yielded yellow crystals of 1.",
